&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-family: &#39;Instrument Sans&#39;, &#39;Segoe UI&#39;, Trebuchet MS, Tahoma, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Vast is developing next-generation space stations and space infrastructure using an incremental, hardware-rich, and capital-efficient approach. Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station to support a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and supporting a growing space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to design, build, and operate its own spacecraft in orbit. Next, Haven-1 is targeted to become the world’s first commercial space station, with launch anticipated in 2027, followed by additional Haven modules. Additionally, the company recently announced two new offerings leveraging its space station components and the heritage of Haven Demo: Vast Satellite, a high-power satellite product line; and Vast Lunar Systems, power, communications, and habitats for the Moon.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in Long Beach, California, and with more than 1,000 employees and over a billion dollars in private capital, Vast has built the facilities capable of manufacturing America’s next space station. The company plans to develop future habitats and systems for Mars, dedicated modules for government partners, and other crewed systems designed to unlock the expanding long-term space economy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast recherche un(e) &lt;strong&gt;Directeur(trice), Développement Commercial International - Satellites&lt;/strong&gt;, sous la responsabilité du &lt;strong&gt;SVP, Satellite Business Development &amp;amp; Commercialization&lt;/strong&gt;, pour diriger le développement commercial axé sur le commerce (communications, observation de la Terre, détection, défense et applications de calcul en orbite) et les gouvernements internationaux pour Vast Satellites. Ce rôle est centré sur les marchés hors États-Unis — notamment l&#39;Europe, le Moyen-Orient et l&#39;Asie — et dirigera l&#39;engagement client, le développement des opportunités, la stratégie de capture, l&#39;engagement gouvernemental/défense et les efforts de partenariat qui font progresser les initiatives de Vast pour développer, fabriquer et exploiter des plateformes de bus satellites avancées.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Il s&#39;agit d&#39;une petite équipe commerciale fondatrice de haut niveau : le rôle exige à la fois des instincts de « hunter » en développement commercial (créer des marchés et de la demande là où il n&#39;en existe pas encore) et des compétences avérées de « closer » (négocier et exécuter des contrats allant de quelques millions à des centaines de millions de dollars).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ce poste sera à &lt;strong&gt;temps plein, exempté&lt;/strong&gt;, ouvert à un lieu de travail international flexible comme décrit ci-dessus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsabilités :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Élaborer et exécuter une stratégie globale de marché commercial et gouvernemental international couvrant l&#39;Europe, le Moyen-Orient et l&#39;Asie, alignée sur les objectifs commerciaux de Vast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Établir et maintenir une veille stratégique sur le marché et la concurrence concernant les clients spatiaux commerciaux et gouvernementaux internationaux, en distinguant le positionnement de Vast de celui de ses concurrents dans chaque région.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Piloter la planification interne pour la priorisation des opportunités internationales, la stratégie de capture et le développement du pipeline sur de multiples marchés alliés et partenaires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diriger l&#39;engagement client à travers l&#39;identification d&#39;opportunités, la définition du périmètre des missions, les présentations de capacités et le développement de concepts précoces avec les opérateurs commerciaux internationaux, les sociétés d&#39;observation de la Terre, les ministères de la défense et les entités gouvernementales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tirer parti d&#39;un solide réseau préexistant de haut niveau au sein de la chaîne de valeur internationale de l&#39;espace et de la défense pour ouvrir des portes auprès de clients potentiels et identifier précocement les menaces concurrentielles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diriger l&#39;élaboration des propositions et coordonner les contributions interfonctionnelles des équipes d&#39;ingénierie, de gestion de programme, de finance, juridique et de contrôle des exportations/conformité, avec le soutien de l&#39;analyste BD et de l&#39;ingénieur avant-vente de l&#39;équipe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assumer la responsabilité du développement du pipeline, des prévisions et des rapports pour tous les comptes commerciaux et gouvernementaux internationaux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Négocier et conclure des contrats pour des missions commerciales et gouvernementales/défense internationales et les services associés, en naviguant à travers divers cadres nationaux de passation de marchés, de contrôle des exportations (ex. ITAR/EAR) et de partenariat.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Se coordonner avec l&#39;équipe de sécurité nationale de Vast lorsque les programmes internationaux croisent des parties prenantes ou des enjeux liés au gouvernement américain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Représenter Vast lors d&#39;événements de l&#39;industrie spatiale, aérospatiale et de défense internationale en Europe, au Moyen-Orient et en Asie.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Faire des présentations, participer à des panels et fournir des briefings de haut niveau/C-suite communiquant les capacités et la valeur des plateformes satellites de Vast aux audiences commerciales, gouvernementales et de défense internationales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications Minimales :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plus de 12 ans d&#39;expérience pertinente dans le développement commercial spatial/aérospatial, les ventes, la gestion de capture ou les contrats gouvernementaux/défense, avec un succès avéré en Europe, au Moyen-Orient et/ou en Asie.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Historique avéré d&#39;origination et de conclusion personnelle de contrats, y compris des transactions de plusieurs dizaines de millions de dollars ou plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relations établies et vérifiables avec des clients potentiels au niveau cadre et exécutif, et connaissance du paysage concurrentiel sur de multiples marchés spatiaux et de défense internationaux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expérience dans la chaîne de valeur spatiale/aérospatiale (lancement, bus satellite, charge utile, intégration maître d&#39;œuvre ou opérations), idéalement complémentaire des opérations satellites — par ex. observation de la Terre ou défense internationale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compréhension approfondie des structures de passation de marchés et de partenariat gouvernementales internationales pertinentes pour les programmes d&#39;espace et de défense.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solides compétences techniques et capacité à communiquer des systèmes complexes à des audiences commerciales, de défense et gouvernementales internationales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellentes capacités de communication, d&#39;analyse, de collaboration et de relations interpersonnelles ; à l&#39;aise pour opérer à travers diverses cultures et langues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacité à opérer de manière autonome, à hiérarchiser les priorités efficacement et à gérer simultanément plusieurs projets internationaux dans un environnement de petite équipe au rythme soutenu.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compétences et Expériences Souhaitées :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relations et crédibilité établies en Europe, au Moyen-Orient et en Asie.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maîtrise des langues pertinentes pour les marchés cibles (français, arabe, japonais, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expérience de travail aux côtés d&#39;équipes d&#39;affaires publiques locales ou coordination avec celles-ci (ex. affaires publiques gouvernementales françaises/UE).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connaissance des régimes de contrôle des exportations (ITAR/EAR) dans les programmes de satellites internationaux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exigences Supplémentaires :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacité à voyager plus de 50 % du temps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Director, Satellite Business Development International&lt;/strong&gt;, reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;SVP, Satellite Business Development &amp;amp; Commercialization&lt;/strong&gt;, to lead commercial (communications, Earth observation, sensing, defense, and in-orbit compute applications) and international government-focused business development for Vast Satellites. This role is focused on markets outside the United States — including Europe, the Middle East, and Asia — and will lead customer engagement, opportunity development, capture strategy, government/defense engagement, and partnership efforts that advance Vast&#39;s initiatives to develop, manufacture, and operate advanced satellite bus platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a small, senior founding commercial team: the role demands both business development &quot;hunter&quot; instincts (creating markets and demand where none exist yet) and proven &quot;closer&quot; skills (negotiating and executing contracts from single-digit millions to hundreds of millions of dollars).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time, exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position open to a flexible international location as described above.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a comprehensive international commercial and government market strategy spanning Europe, the Middle East, and Asia, aligned with Vast&#39;s business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a market and competitive intelligence view across international commercial and government space customers, distinguishing Vast&#39;s positioning from competitors in each region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead internal planning for international opportunity prioritization, capture strategy, and pipeline development across multiple allied and partner markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead customer engagement across opportunity identification, mission scoping, capability briefings, and early concept development with international commercial operators, Earth observation companies, defense ministries, and government entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage a strong, pre-existing senior-level network across the international space/defense value chain to open doors with potential customers and identify competitive threats early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead proposal development and coordinate cross-functional contributions from engineering, program management, finance, legal, and export-control/compliance teams, supported by the team&#39;s BD analyst and pre-sales engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own pipeline development, forecasting, and reporting across all international commercial and government accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate and close contracts for international commercial and government/defense missions and associated services, navigating varying national procurement, export-control (e.g., ITAR/EAR), and partnership frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Vast&#39;s National Security team where international programs intersect with US Government stakeholders or content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Vast at international space, aerospace, and defense industry events across Europe, the Middle East, and Asia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver presentations, participate in panels, and provide senior/C-suite-level briefings that communicate the capabilities and value of Vast&#39;s satellite platforms to international commercial, government, and defense audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of relevant experience in space/aerospace business development, sales, capture management, or government/defense contracting, with demonstrated success operating in Europe, the Middle East, and/or Asia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of personally originating and closing contracts, including deals in the tens of millions of dollars or above.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established, verifiable senior and executive-level relationships with potential customers, and knowledge of the competitive landscape across multiple international space/defense markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in the space/aerospace value chain (launch, satellite bus, payload, prime integration, or operations), ideally complementary to satellite operations — e.g., Earth observation or international defense.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of international government procurement and partnership structures relevant to space and defense programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical understanding and ability to communicate complex systems to international commercial, defense, and government audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, analytical, collaboration, and interpersonal skills; comfortable operating across cultures and languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently, prioritize effectively, and manage multiple international efforts simultaneously in a fast-paced, lean-team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships and credibility across Europe, the Middle East, and Asia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in languages relevant to target markets (French, Arabic, Japanese, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working alongside or coordinating with in-country government affairs teams (e.g., French/EU government affairs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with export-control regimes (ITAR/EAR) in international satellite programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel 50%+ of the time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-family: &#39;Instrument Sans&#39;, &#39;Segoe UI&#39;, Trebuchet MS, Tahoma, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We calibrate level and compensation to the selected candidate&#39;s experience and demonstrated capability. We welcome applicants across a range of experience levels to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base salary will vary depending on job-related knowledge, education, skills, experience, business needs, and market demand. Salary is just one component of our comprehensive compensation package. Full-time employees also receive company equity, as well as access to a full suite of compelling benefits and perks, including: medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents, generous paid time off; up to 20+ days of vacation for exempt staff and up to 10+ days of vacation for non-exempt staff with the ability to cash-out unused vacation annually, paid parental leave, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, ClassPass credits, personalized mental healthcare through Spring Health, and other discounts and perks. We also take pride in offering exceptional food perks, with snacks, drip coffee &amp;amp; onsite barista, cold drinks, and dinner meals remaining free of charge, and lunch subsidized as part of Vast’s ongoing commitment to providing high-quality meals for employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EQUAL OPPORTUNITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Vast is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with Vast is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2 class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-section-id=&quot;1dfch1y&quot; data-start=&quot;216&quot; data-end=&quot;232&quot;&gt;About the job&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;234&quot; data-end=&quot;321&quot;&gt;Lead the team that proves our AI silicon performs reliably before it reaches customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;323&quot; data-end=&quot;527&quot;&gt;You will build and lead Graphcore&#39;s characterisation capability for next generation silicon and system platforms. Your work will help ensure our products perform consistently across real world conditions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;529&quot; data-end=&quot;790&quot;&gt;You will define bring up and characterisation strategies, lead technical execution, and shape the lab infrastructure needed for success. You&#39;ll work across silicon, hardware, manufacturing, architecture and product teams to solve complex engineering challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;792&quot; data-end=&quot;927&quot;&gt;This is a hands on leadership role with the opportunity to influence both product design and how Graphcore validates future AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;1pc0zxi&quot; data-start=&quot;929&quot; data-end=&quot;952&quot;&gt;The team and culture&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;954&quot; data-end=&quot;1144&quot;&gt;This is a newly formed team within Manufacturing Operations. You&#39;ll have the opportunity to establish how the team works while building strong partnerships across engineering and operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1146&quot; data-end=&quot;1343&quot;&gt;Day to day, you&#39;ll work closely with architecture, silicon, hardware, production test and product teams. Decisions are driven by data, technical evidence and close collaboration across disciplines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1345&quot; data-end=&quot;1497&quot;&gt;We value ownership and clear communication. You&#39;ll be trusted to lead technical direction, remove blockers and help teams make progress with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;hsl8wh&quot; data-start=&quot;1499&quot; data-end=&quot;1524&quot;&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Essential&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1cwxr2j&quot; data-start=&quot;0&quot; data-end=&quot;181&quot;&gt;Proven track record of delivering complex technical projects as an individual contributor, manager, or project manager, with the ability to work independently and drive execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1bbmz19&quot; data-start=&quot;182&quot; data-end=&quot;379&quot;&gt;Strong expertise in silicon digital device design, bring-up, characterisation, and silicon process technologies, with an understanding of their impact on transistor- and system-level performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1af93xd&quot; data-start=&quot;380&quot; data-end=&quot;535&quot;&gt;In-depth knowledge of high-performance processors, system-on-chip (SoC) architectures, and high-speed digital interfaces such as PCIe, Ethernet, and DDR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;88mybm&quot; data-start=&quot;536&quot; data-end=&quot;719&quot;&gt;Experience with measurement automation, data analysis, and scripting/coding to develop automated test and analysis workflows, with familiarity of ATE systems and their capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1i7iazr&quot; data-start=&quot;720&quot; data-end=&quot;866&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot;&gt;Excellent communication, presentation, and stakeholder management skills, supported by a bachelor&#39;s degree (or equivalent practical experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Desirable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;11&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;multilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;20&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Knowledge of PCBA and system level technologies.  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;11&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;multilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;20&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Project management experience.  &lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;hsl8wh&quot; data-start=&quot;1499&quot; data-end=&quot;1524&quot;&gt;Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;2111&quot; data-end=&quot;2482&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;s6bpph&quot; data-start=&quot;2111&quot; data-end=&quot;2135&quot;&gt;Unlimited annual leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1xdcm9g&quot; data-start=&quot;2136&quot; data-end=&quot;2162&quot;&gt;Up to 5% matched pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;9i84tx&quot; data-start=&quot;2163&quot; data-end=&quot;2210&quot;&gt;Phantom equity – share in Graphcore&#39;s success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;29x8ds&quot; data-start=&quot;2211&quot; data-end=&quot;2255&quot;&gt;True flexibility in how and where you work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;18jz13s&quot; data-start=&quot;2256&quot; data-end=&quot;2298&quot;&gt;Office spaces designed for collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;ywp1yb&quot; data-start=&quot;2299&quot; data-end=&quot;2333&quot;&gt;Free food and an on-site barista&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;vtixha&quot; data-start=&quot;2334&quot; data-end=&quot;2352&quot;&gt;Health cash plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1pdwmtk&quot; data-start=&quot;2353&quot; data-end=&quot;2372&quot;&gt;Income protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;4nbmbl&quot; data-start=&quot;2373&quot; data-end=&quot;2389&quot;&gt;Life assurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;150wh0j&quot; data-start=&quot;2390&quot; data-end=&quot;2482&quot;&gt;Along with other benefits you can choose from (private medical insurance, dental plan etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2484&quot; data-end=&quot;2632&quot;&gt;We welcome people from all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2634&quot; data-end=&quot;2846&quot;&gt;We&#39;re an equal opportunity employer and recognise that everyone brings different strengths and perspectives. If you need any adjustments during the interview process, just let us know. We&#39;re happy to support you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;48xncx&quot; data-start=&quot;2848&quot; data-end=&quot;2877&quot;&gt;Join the team at Graphcore&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2879&quot; data-end=&quot;3119&quot;&gt;Graphcore is building the compute platform for the next generation of artificial intelligence. From advanced silicon to intelligent software, our technology is designed to unlock breakthroughs in AI and bring its benefits to every industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3121&quot; data-end=&quot;3413&quot;&gt;As part of the SoftBank Group, we&#39;re backed by one of the world&#39;s most ambitious technology investors, working alongside companies shaping the future of AI. Together, we share a bold goal: to help enable artificial superintelligence and ensure it delivers meaningful impact at a global scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3415&quot; data-end=&quot;3865&quot;&gt;At Graphcore, you&#39;ll work with people who are pushing the boundaries of what&#39;s possible. Our teams bring together AI researchers, chip designers, software engineers and systems experts from a wide range of backgrounds. It&#39;s an environment where we take on big challenges with curiosity and focus, move quickly and decisively, take real ownership of our work, and speak up to challenge ideas, stepping up to support each other and lead through action.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3867&quot; data-end=&quot;4064&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-is-only-node=&quot;&quot;&gt;If you want to lead the team that validates the technology powering the next generation of AI systems, we&#39;d love to hear from you. Apply now to join Graphcore.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3867&quot; data-end=&quot;4064&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-is-only-node=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Elastic, the Search AI Company, enables everyone to find the answers they need in real time, using all their data, at scale — unleashing the potential of businesses and people. The Elastic Search AI Platform, used by more than 50% of the Fortune 500, brings together the precision of search and the intelligence of AI to enable everyone to accelerate the results that matter. By taking advantage of all structured and unstructured data — securing and protecting private information more effectively — Elastic’s complete, cloud-based solutions for search, security, and observability help organizations deliver on the promise of AI.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Elastic is looking for an exceptional delivery consulting leader — someone who has built and run international delivery organisations, understands how to drive bookings growth and revenue expansion inside complex enterprise accounts, and can operate at the highest levels of client engagement while simultaneously leading and transforming a mid-sized, globally distributed team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the international Delivery Management function across Elastic Professional Services — leading the team, driving the transformation, and acting as the senior client presence on our most strategic engagements. You will be accountable for both the operational health of the delivery organisation and the commercial outcomes it generates: bookings, revenue, and margin across EMEA and APJ.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Delivery excellence is your foundation. Commercial growth is your north star. Building the team that industrialises both — and equips it for an AI-enabled future — is your legacy.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Doing&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;International Delivery Organisation — EMEA &amp;amp; APJ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Own and lead the international Delivery Management function&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; a team of ~15 Delivery Managers today, distributed across global delivery hubs in EMEA and APJ — with a clear mandate and expectation to scale substantially through 2027 and 2028 as the practice grows and demand accelerates across both regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; Drive a team transformation &lt;/strong&gt;— reframing how Delivery Managers operate, shifting from project execution to outcome-led consulting, equipping the team to hold more strategic client conversations and drive greater account value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Champion and drive the adoption of Fixed Price engagement models&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; leading the organisation through the commercial, contractual, and delivery discipline required to scope, price, and execute fixed-price engagements with confidence, especially with platform migrations — protecting margin while driving predictable, high-quality client outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; Build a dual-mode delivery capability that operates with excellence across two distinct motions:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;①&amp;nbsp; Packaged Solutions&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; —&amp;nbsp; fast, repeatable, industrialised delivery of high-value outcome-based offerings at scale — anchored in Fixed Price commercial models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;②&amp;nbsp; Transformative Engagements&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; —&amp;nbsp; large, complex migrations and solution delivery that require senior delivery governance, deep client partnership, and adaptive programme leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Lead the integration of AI into the Delivery Management function&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; identifying and embedding AI-powered tools and practices that improve team productivity, sharpen delivery insight, and — critically — enrich the client experience by enabling more proactive, personalised, and higher-value engagement throughout the delivery lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Design and embed delivery standards, frameworks, and tooling&lt;/strong&gt; — including AI-augmented capabilities — that enable the team to scale both delivery modes without sacrificing quality or client outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; Act as a player-coach&lt;/strong&gt; — maintaining direct governance oversight on the most complex or at-risk international engagements, intervening and course-correcting where needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; Build a coaching and development culture within the team&lt;/strong&gt; — raising the floor on delivery craft and the ceiling on consulting commerciality across every region working closely with the Regional Services Directors, to generate new opportunities on the back of outstanding delivery.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Leadership &amp;amp; Commercial Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Own financial accountability across the international delivery portfolio&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; driving consulting bookings growth from delivery, maximising revenue realisation from engagements, and actively improving delivery margin through disciplined engagement management, Fixed Price adoption, and commercial rigour.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Grow the consulting footprint&lt;/strong&gt; within a portfolio of strategic enterprise accounts across EMEA and APJ, driving land-and-expand value outcomes in close partnership with regional Sales organisations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Build and sustain C-level and VP-level executive relationships&lt;/strong&gt; that extend beyond the project — becoming the trusted advisor clients return to for their most important decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸ &lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Develop compelling value narratives&lt;/strong&gt; that articulate the value of engaging Elastic&#39;s consulting services, influencing renewal, expansion, and new commercial commitments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸ &lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Partner with Regional Services Directors on pipeline development&lt;/strong&gt; — acting as a senior consulting delivery voice in pre-sales conversations, solution framing, and commercial structuring including Fixed Price proposals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional &amp;amp; Organisational Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; Serve as the connective tissue between Consulting, Sales, Customer Success, and Product when driving an engagement — ensuring a unified client experience and shared accountability for outcomes across EMEA and APJ.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; Contribute to the evolution of Elastic&#39;s delivery consulting go-to-market: methodology design, packaged solution development, delivery model innovation, AI-enabled tooling, and commercial frameworks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; Represent Elastic Professional Services at the senior leadership level — internally and externally — with the credibility and presence to influence how the organisation grows internationally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;International enterprise leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; Proven track record building and leading delivery teams across EMEA and/or APJ. You understand how regional culture, client expectations, and hub-based delivery dynamics shape outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Fixed Price engagement expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; You have designed, sold, and delivered Fixed Price consulting engagements at scale. You understand the scoping rigour, risk management, and delivery discipline required to make this model work — and you have driven its adoption across a delivery organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Financial accountability&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; You have owned a P&amp;amp;L or delivery portfolio with direct accountability for bookings, revenue, and margin — and you have a track record of improving all three.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Dual-mode delivery experience&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; You have designed and operated delivery models that handle both high-velocity repeatable engagements and complex, multi-stakeholder transformations — simultaneously.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;AI fluency in a delivery context&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; You have a clear point of view on how AI can transform delivery management and client engagement — and you have practical experience applying AI tools to improve team effectiveness, delivery quality, or customer outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Commercial acumen&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; You have expanded client accounts, shaped SOWs, and driven revenue growth from within a delivery or consulting organisation. You know how value conversations are won.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Executive presence&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; You are credible at the C-suite level across multiple geographies. You have built relationships that outlast individual projects and turned delivery success into long-term strategic partnership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;People leadership at scale&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; You have led and transformed mid-to-large delivery teams, building coaching cultures that raise performance and commerciality across a distributed, multi-timezone workforce.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;12+ years&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; in management consulting, professional services, or enterprise SaaS delivery leadership — with meaningful time spent in both client-facing growth roles and people/org leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; Experience industrialising packaged service offerings — creating repeatable, Fixed Price delivery motions from complex, bespoke prior engagements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; Hands-on experience deploying AI tools within a professional services or consulting delivery environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; Background spanning pre-sales/solutioning and post-sales delivery — the full consulting lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; Experience with enterprise SaaS platforms (e.g. Elastic, Salesforce, ServiceNow, Databricks) in a consulting or professional services capacity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; Agile and hybrid delivery framework fluency in complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise environments, but with extensive experience of platform migrations / tools consolidation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▸&amp;nbsp; Certifications (PMP, CSM, or equivalent) are valued, though leadership track record and client outcomes matter more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Elastic&#39;s Professional Services organisation is at an inflection point internationally. We are scaling a delivery team across EMEA and APJ — with significant headcount growth expected through 2027 and 2028 — building a dual-mode delivery capability, shifting to Fixed Price engagement models, embedding AI into how we deliver and engage clients, and growing a client base that demands senior, outcome-focused leadership. All at once.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role carries real financial weight and a real transformation mandate. You will have the authority to reshape how an international team operates, the commercial platform to build lasting client partnerships across two major regions, and the executive visibility to influence how Elastic goes to market with its consulting capability globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have built delivery organisations, owned the numbers, led through transformation, embraced AI as a genuine force multiplier, and made Fixed Price work where others haven&#39;t — and you are looking for a role where all of it matters — this is it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Information - We Take Care of Our People&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a distributed company, diversity drives our identity. Whether you’re looking to launch a new career or grow an existing one, Elastic is the type of company where you can balance great work with great life. Your age is only a number. It doesn’t matter if you’re just out of college or your children are; we need you for what you can do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strive to have parity of benefits across regions and while regulations differ from place to place, we believe taking care of our people is the right thing to do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive pay based on the work you do here and not your previous salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health coverage for you and your family in many locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to craft your calendar with flexible locations and schedules for many roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous number of vacation days each year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increase your impact - We match up to $2000 (or local currency equivalent) for financial donations and service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to 40 hours each year to use toward volunteer projects you love&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embracing parenthood with minimum of 16 weeks of parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Different people approach problems differently. We need that. Elastic is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating an inclusive culture that celebrates different perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, ethnicity, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender perception or identity, national origin, age, marital status, protected veteran status, disability status, or any other basis protected by federal, state or local law, ordinance or regulation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome individuals with disabilities and strive to create an accessible and inclusive experience for all individuals. To request an accommodation during the application or the recruiting process, please email &lt;a ----- ----- class=&quot;gmail_default&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;We will reply to your request within 24 business hours of submission.&lt;/p&gt;
